  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing Partner Capacity to Support Zimbabwe Country Strategy Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To make sure that new projects and programmes conform with the Strategic Plan, field assessments, social analyses, and baseline evaluations need to be conducted. These will assist in understanding the context in which the new programmes are being implemented. Social analyses conducted during field assessments will identify the target communities&apos; most pressing needs and priorities. Baseline evaluations will provide a starting point against which project progress can be measured. Field assessments, social analyses, and baseline evaluations will contribute to transparency, accountability, and learning throughout the project cycle. The data and insights gathered through field assessments, social analyses, and baseline evaluations provide a strong foundation for evidence-based decision-making.</narrative>
  </description>
